	A notion or two (I don't pretend to KNOW the answers... This
is speculation. You have been warned.)
	Perhaps to mollify your god, you need some really spectacular
sacrifice. As your character gains levels, a relatively easy to kill
monster like an Uruk-Hai may be worth less and less in your god's eyes.
Have you sacrificed anything really mean, like a dragon or a troll
lately?
	This is just a thought, again: could there be a problem with
alignment rollover, that is, if you are too good to your god, could
your alignment "wrap around" to become negative?
	Finally, you must have done something to make your god angry.
Praying too often will do it; killing friendly creatures will do it.
If you have done either of these things, well, don't do them again.
	There is, most likely, a random factor involved in determining
the acceptability of a sacrifice. You could just be having the world's
worst luck, I suppose.
